  - id: the_man_of_sin
    displayName: The Man of Sin
    flavorText: Paul teaches that the day of Christ will not come until a falling
      away occurs and the man of sin is revealed, exalting himself above God until
      the Lord consumes him with the breath of his mouth.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Corrects a false report or letter falsely claiming Paul's authorship,
      which asserted the day of Christ had already come. Paul teaches that a falling
      away must occur first and the man of sin, the son of perdition, must be revealed
      and exalt himself above God, restrained for now until the restrainer is taken
      out of the way, after which the Lord Jesus will destroy him at his coming.
    deliveredByManagerId: paul_2thessalonians
