  - id: working_with_quietness
    displayName: Working with Quietness
    flavorText: Paul commands the church to withdraw from any brother who walks disorderly
      and refuses to work, urging the disorderly instead to labor quietly and eat
      their own bread.
    tierType: 1
    purpose: Addresses members who were walking disorderly, refusing to work, and
      acting as busybodies, likely stirred by end-times excitement. Paul commands
      the church to withdraw from any brother who will not follow this teaching,
      restates 'if any would not work, neither should he eat,' and instructs offenders
      to be admonished as brothers rather than treated as enemies.
    deliveredByManagerId: paul_2thessalonians
